Portions of this repository are derived from that work, including:

  - src/aoi_pcb_ssd/model/ssd_custom.py
  - src/aoi_pcb_ssd/model/ssd_transfer.py
    Derived from upstream models/keras_ssd7.py.
    The feature extractor, three-branch detection head (classification,
    corner-offset regression, grid-centre encoding), and overall model
    structure are modifications introduced for this work. The custom CNN
    backbone (6 convolutional blocks, 5x5 kernels in the first two blocks)
    and the use of grid-centre anchors instead of aspect-ratio bounding
    boxes are original contributions described in the accompanying paper.

  - src/aoi_pcb_ssd/model/loss.py
    Derived from upstream keras_loss_function/keras_ssd_loss.py.
    Adapted for TensorFlow 2. The localization loss is replaced with a
    custom L1/L2 hybrid and the regression target is an eight-coordinate
    four-corner-point representation rather than the standard (cx, cy, w, h)
    bounding box format.

  - src/aoi_pcb_ssd/encoding/input_encoder.py
  - src/aoi_pcb_ssd/encoding/output_decoder.py
    Derived from upstream ssd_encoder_decoder/ssd_input_encoder.py and
    ssd_output_decoder.py respectively.
    Matching strategy changed from IoU-based to nearest-centre distance.
    Regression targets encode four corner points per object instead of
    bounding box offsets.

  - src/aoi_pcb_ssd/model/grid_centers.py
    Derived from upstream keras_layers/keras_layer_AnchorBoxes.py.
    Produces only the (cx, cy) centre coordinates of each feature map cell,
    omitting the width, height, and variance fields of the original anchor
    box layer.
